\paragraph{Answer to the second question: lexical selection.}
The query-entity selector reversed the keyword filter's failure. Full-context accuracy was \pruningFullAccuracy{}\%, compared with \pruningPrunedAccuracy{}\% after keyword filtering and \entitySelectorAccuracy{}\% after query-entity selection. Against full context, query-entity selection produced \entitySelectorWins{} wins, \entitySelectorLosses{} losses, and \entitySelectorTies{} ties across \entitySelectorDenominator{} cases from \entitySelectorFamilyCount{} families. Against keyword pruning, it gained \selectorComparisonChange{} points, with \selectorComparisonWins{} wins, \selectorComparisonLosses{} losses, and \selectorComparisonTies{} ties over the same family count (Table~\ref{tab:pruning}).

